<title>ESTONIA: HANSAINVEST SEEKS TO ADVISE LITHUANIA: REPORT.</title>
<headline>HANSAINVEST SEEKS TO ADVISE LITHUANIA: REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hansa Investments and a London- based investment bank, Flemings, has approached the Lithuanian government seeking to be consultants for the privatisation of Lithuanian Telecom, Aripaev business daily said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Before inviting bids for Lithuanian Telecom, the government will choose an advisor,&quot; Joakim Helenius, chairman of Hansa Invesments said in Aripaev.</p>
<p>Combined with Flemings, Hansa Investments see its bid as a strong one, Helenius added.</p>
<p>The market value of the shares of Lithianian Telecom could worth as much as one billion dollars, he said in the paper.</p>
<p>Flemings has strong interest in new and emerging markets and is a world-wide advisor in privatsation.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom, 372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
